#
# Citation metadata for GitHub's "Cite this repository" and for Zenodo, which
# archives every GitHub Release of this repository. No version or release date
# here on purpose: Zenodo takes them from the release tag, so this file never
# goes stale (KOF-450).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KoFEM in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: KoFEM
abstract: >-
  KoFEM is a finite element analysis tool that runs entirely in the web
  browser, without installation and without sending model data to a server.
  It runs the full pipeline from STEP geometry through OCCT and Netgen
  meshing to a finite-element solve: geometry and meshing in a C++ engine
  and the solver in Rust, both compiled to WebAssembly, with a React and
  Three.js frontend.
authors:
  - given-names: Michael
    family-names: Kofler
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/mkofler96/KoFEM"
url: "https://kofem.org"
keywords:
  - finite element analysis
  - finite element method
  - structural analysis
  - WebAssembly
  - browser
  - mesh generation
  - shell elements
  - topology optimization
